1. VOIDOS ORIGINAL WORKS

"VoidOS Original Works" means the material authored by the VoidOS Project,
including:

  (a) the VoidOS applications and daemons (void-panel, void-settings,
      void-power, void-update, void-disks, void-wizard, void-installer,
      void-shutdown-ui and the other void-* components);
  (b) the VoidOS build system, phase scripts, packaging definitions and
      verification invariants;
  (c) the VoidOS theme, stylesheets, artwork and documentation;
  (d) the VoidOS name, logo and visual identity (see Section 6).

It does NOT mean the third-party software described in Section 5, even where
that software has been configured, patched or packaged by the VoidOS Project.


2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

You may, at no charge:

  (a) install and run VoidOS on any number of devices you own or control, for
      any purpose, personal or commercial;
  (b) modify VoidOS on your own devices, to any extent, for your own use —
      including editing configuration, replacing components, and building a
      modified image for yourself;
  (c) redistribute an OFFICIAL, UNMODIFIED VoidOS image, provided it is
      bit-for-bit identical to a release published by the VoidOS Project, is
      accompanied by this License, and retains all notices, signatures and
      checksums intact;
  (d) study the VoidOS Original Works where they are published, and discuss,
      review, report issues in, and publish analysis of them.


3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Except as Section 5 permits for third-party software, you may not:

  (a) distribute a modified VoidOS image, or any image derived from VoidOS, to
      any third party;
  (b) distribute the VoidOS Original Works, in source or binary form, separately
      from an official unmodified image;
  (c) sell, sublicense, rent or offer VoidOS as a paid product or paid service;
  (d) remove, alter or obscure any copyright notice, license text, signature or
      integrity check;
  (e) represent a modified system as being VoidOS, or as endorsed by, verified
      by, or originating from the VoidOS Project.

Clause (a) restricts DISTRIBUTION only. Modifying your own device is expressly
permitted by Section 2(b) and nothing here limits it.


4. INTEGRITY

VoidOS publishes a SHA-256 checksum and a cryptographic signature for each
release, and the operating system verifies them before applying an update.
Circumventing, disabling or falsifying these mechanisms in a copy you
distribute to others is prohibited. Disabling them on your own device is your
choice and your risk.


